<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!-- Base application theme. -->
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="Theme.AppCompat.Light.DarkActionBar">
        <!-- Customize your theme here. -->
        <item name="colorPrimary">@color/colorPrimary</item>
        <item name="colorPrimaryDark">@color/colorPrimaryDark</item>
        <item name="colorAccent">@color/colorAccent</item>
    </style>

    <!--
      The theme the activity runs in AFTER the splash hands over.

      android:windowBackground is the line that matters, and it was not
      here. The android:background below it is a VIEW attribute; on a theme
      it does nothing to the window, so the window background fell through
      to Theme.AppCompat.DayNight's ?android:colorBackground, which is white
      in light mode.

      That was invisible until now only because the launch theme never
      handed over: with no postSplashScreenTheme the activity kept the
      launch theme and its drawable for the whole session. Adding the
      handoff below is what opens the white frame this line closes.
    -->
    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBar" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <item name="windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="windowNoTitle">true</item>
        <item name="android:background">@null</item>
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/splash_background</item>
    </style>


    <!--
      ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
      THE LAUNCH THEME
      ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

      What was here was one line, android:background="@drawable/splash",
      and on Android 12 and later the platform ignores it completely. Since
      Android 12 the system draws the splash itself from windowSplashScreen
      attributes, and an app that sets none of them gets the default: the
      launcher icon on ?android:colorBackground. So this app's launch screen
      was a tile on white for every phone shipped since 2021, and the ten
      densities of splash.png that render-app-icons.mjs writes per flavour
      were never once drawn.

      These are the COMPAT attribute names, without the android: prefix.
      androidx.core:core-splashscreen reads them itself on API 24 to 30 and
      maps them onto the platform attributes on 31 and up. values-v31 sets
      the platform ones explicitly on top; see the note in that file.

      postSplashScreenTheme is not optional and is the one people omit. It
      is what installSplashScreen() applies when the splash leaves. Without
      it the activity keeps THIS theme, and the splash stays behind the
      WebView for the life of the process.
    -->
    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBarLaunch" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/splash_background</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_icon_blank</item>
        <!--
          Zero, because splash_icon_blank has nothing to animate. The
          platform caps this at 1000 and any value here only delays the
          handoff to the real launch screen, which is what the app is
          trying to show as early as possible.
        -->
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimationDuration">0</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/AppTheme.NoActionBar</item>
    </style>
</resources>